    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0046" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/1–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Mission for Aid to Greece
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-12T19:00:00-05:00">January 12, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gama 41.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d11-f1"/> For
                    Griswold and Embassy. Destruction guerrilla forces and establishment internal
                    security (further to Gama 718<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d11-f2"/>) now have clearly assumed paramount importance as
                    necessary preliminary for successful American aid to Greece. Until achieved <hi
                        rendition="#italic">these aims should</hi> henceforth take precedence over
                    any portions present program which do not directly support <hi
                        rendition="#italic">them. Dept. would therefore view favorably any program
                        modifications you may recommend after re-examining Mission projects in terms
                        of their furtherance, with least delay, of this basic objective</hi>.</p>
                <pb facs="0047" n="27" xml:id="pg27"/>
                <p>Foregoing also underlies JCS directive to
                    Livesay, copy of which being air pouched to you and Emb.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d11-f1" n="1" xml:id="d11-f1-content">
                <p>Sent originally, also as Gama 41, on January 9.
                    The additions in the January 12 version are italicized.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d11-f2" n="2" xml:id="d11-f2-content">
                <p>Dated December 30, 1947, <ref target="frus1947v05#pg_478">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1947, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, p. 478</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
